    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), touching three files with minimal, cohesive edits:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string property with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getMembershipLevel()`/`setMembershipLevel(Integer)` and drops the old field from the response.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 changed the single `@Mapping` expression to compute the level: `Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))`. Start at 1, +1 for email, +1 for no namesakes, capped at 3.\n\n3. **`HouseholdTier.java`** \u2014 the household-of-3+ override previously set the tier to `\"GOLD\"`; updated the one line to `setMembershipLevel(3)` (top of the standard range, preserving that a full household reaches the highest non-tenure level).\n\nThe create audit line (`AuditOwnerCreated`) records `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 it never recorded the tier \u2014 so nothing there needed changing.\n\nEach edit is a one-line change in a small, low-complexity function, keeping structural impact minimal. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (expects level 3 for an owner with email + no namesakes) and the full suite pass.",
